 result←object(State Chord)arg;props;tunits;circle;this;radius;pen;nopen
 result←⍬
 ⍝ 'Chord' r c radius [aspect [start end [border]]]
 ⍝ 'Chord' r c radius [aspect [start end [border]]] ...
 ⍝ 'Chord' n m ⍴ r c radius [aspect [start end [border]]] ,,,

 :If 1≥|≡arg ⋄ arg←,⊂arg ⋄ :EndIf
 '∆WI RANK ERROR: Chord'##.Error∨/2<≢¨⍴¨arg
 '∆WI LENGTH ERROR: Chord'##.Error∨/~(⊢/¨⍴¨arg)∊¨⊂3 4 6 7
 tunits←⊃##.Classes._supp.MyUnits State
 arg←⊃,/,¨↓¨arg ⍝ If any items are matrices, split them into individual lines so we can process them sequentially then recombine into a single matrix
 props←StartObj''
 props,←pen←DefinePen State
 props,←DefineBrush State
 props,←⊂'DrawMode'(2⊃State._mode)
 nopen←,⊂'LStyle' 5 ⍝ In case we need to selectively hide all the lines by overriding the pen type

 :For circle :In arg ⍝ Only build one chord at a time
     circle,←circle≢⍛↓0 0 0 1 0 360 1 ⍝ Assign defaults
     this←(∨/circle[5 6]≠0 360)/↓'Start' 'End',⍤0⊢circle[5 6]×○÷180
     this,←⊂'ArcMode'(⌈/0 1/⍨1 2∊##.Classes._supp.SetBitVals 7⊃circle) ⍝? This does not provide full support - do the best we can
     :If circle[4]∊(÷/⌽tunits),-÷/tunits ⍝ Then they want a perfect circle even with asymmetrical units ⍝? Does this always work?
         this,←⊂'Points'(tunits×2↑circle)
         this,←⊂'Radius'(tunits[2]×circle[3])
         State GUI'Circle'⊂⍛,props,(nopen/⍨circle[7]=0),this
     :Else ⍝ They're asking for an ellipse instead (have to use a bounding rectangle)
         ⍝? Are the pixels themselves considered to be square enough to ignore something like ÷/×/##.GUIRoot.(_AspectRatio _pix_size); separate for Printer?
         radius←circle[3]×⌽tunits×|(circle[4]≥0)⌽1,circle[4] ⍝ Compute relative radii by aspect ratio
         this,←⊂'Points'(1-⍨radius-⍨tunits×2↑circle)
         this,←⊂'Size'(1+2×radius) ⍝ Account for 0-point at center
         State GUI'Ellipse'⊂⍛,props,(nopen/⍨circle[7]=0),this
     :EndIf
 :EndFor
